<Base title="Privacy" description="What Mission Bay News collects from residents, why, and who can see it.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lede">Mission Bay News is run by resident volunteers. We keep what we collect to a minimum.</p>

  <h2>What this website collects</h2>
  <p>Nothing. This website has no accounts and no tracking. Your text-size choice is saved only in your own browser.</p>

  <h2>What the sign-up form collects</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name, space number and email address.</li>
    <li>Your phone number, only if you choose to give it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The form is on a separate service (Google Forms). Answers go to a private spreadsheet that only a small number of named volunteers can open.</p>

  <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
  <p>Only to confirm that you live in Mission Bay and to give you access to the residents' area. We do not sell or share it, and we do not give it to park management or anyone else.</p>

  <h2>The survey</h2>
  <p>The resident survey is anonymous. It does not ask for your name, and we cannot link answers to a person.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>Sign-up answers are deleted once you are approved or declined, and the approved-member list is checked every year. People who move away are removed.</p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>You can ask to see, correct or remove your details, or leave the group, at any time. <a href="/contact/">Contact the editor</a>.</p>

  <h2>Group rules</h2>
  <p>Residents' group posts are for residents only. Please do not share what others post outside the group.</p>
</Base>
